From 77ffd5f35d5baad852c5ec4345c71b6815ec2fa3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:19:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] test: declare long tests `extended` instead of keeping
 timing.json

Which tests were extended came from the checked-in timing.json: any test
over 40 seconds on the machine that last updated it. Tests now say it
themselves: `extended = True`, or the set of variants that are long
(`extended = {"descriptors"}`). The runner leaves them out unless
--extended is given or the test is named on the command line.

The 17 tests over 40 s in timing.json are marked, so the default run is
unchanged, except that feature_index_prune.py is now extended too: under
parallel load it is the longest default test.

timing.json, its update script and --cutoff are removed. The runner still
starts the longest tests first, from the durations it records in the build
directory (test/durations.json), and without them starts the extended ones
first.
